= Foreword

Similar to physics, this is another domain where I have relatively more exposure. Still, because of the rapid pace of development in ML, I have left many holes in my understanding while trying to learn all the cool tricks and new architectures.

Unlike other subjects, ML is relatively new, and there is no clear golden path for study yet. So instead of following a particular book for a specific topic, I am going to do what I would have done if I were still faculty and had to teach a machine learning class: look online and make a "lecture note" for each topic, even though I am not teaching anymore.

Because this is not a course targeting a specific level, the difficulty of each topic may vary significantly. I will indicate the prerequisites needed to understand each note at the top to the best of my ability.

